{"id": "whcomoe", "name": "Comoé National Park", "short": "Comoé", "place": "Côte d'Ivoire", "lat": 9.16, "lon": -3.77, "side": "l", "cont": "Africa", "country": "Côte d'Ivoire", "kind": "Grassland", "park": true, "blurb": "West Africa's largest savanna park: grass, gallery forest, hippos and a river.", "tip": {"id": "kob", "title": "Thin the kob herds", "text": "Kob are a main prey of leopards and hyenas and a carcass source for vultures. Set Kob to -100% and watch the predators, scavengers and the Andropogon grass respond."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Comoé National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comoé_National_Park"}, {"title": "UNESCO World Heritage: Comoé National Park", "url": "https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/227/"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Guinean forest-savanna mosaic", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guinean_forest–savanna_mosaic"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Hippopotamus", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hippopotamus"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Spotted hyena", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spotted_hyena"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: White-backed vulture", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White-backed_vulture"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Comoé National Park", "icon": "grass", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.08, "desc": "Strong tropical sun drives growth of the savanna grasses and trees through the wet season."}, {"id": "rain", "sp": "seasonal rains and river floods", "xh": 0.28}, {"id": "fire", "sp": "dry-season fire", "xh": 0.5, "wiki": "Fire ecology"}, {"id": "soil", "sp": "infertile soils", "xh": 0.7}, {"id": "decomp", "sp": "bacteria and fungi", "xh": 0.92, "desc": "Bacteria, fungi and termites break down dead grass, leaves and carcasses, re